{
  "baseline": {
    "files": [
      "threats.md",
      "risk-scores.md",
      "risk-scores.sarif"
    ],
    "form": "legacy",
    "frontmatter_date": "2026-11-09",
    "note": "pre-fix form with its SARIF; only run1 reads it"
  },
  "flag_reading": [
    "A flag is kind:field:cause, and the field is the value whose status the flag describes, by its schemas/risk-scoring.yaml name: cvss_base, composite_score, severity_band, remediation_sla, risk_disposition, review_date, reachability.",
    "The cause of a 'corrected' flag names the step that produced the field's new value: a changed cvss_base is 'vector', a changed composite_score is 'arithmetic', a changed severity_band is 'band-mapping' (or 'rounding' when only rounding moved the band), and a changed remediation_sla, risk_disposition or review_date is 'follows-band'. Where a fallback set the review date, 'baseline-date' or 'clock-restarted' replaces 'follows-band'. A change that the asset tags alone explain takes 'retagged' and the cause 'asset-tags' on every field it moves (ruling A). A finding carries at most one flag per kind and field.",
    "A rounding-only composite difference is normalized and counted and never flagged: only a band that it moves is flagged, as severity_band:rounding.",
    "basis 'pinned': the string is in the closed vocabulary of contracts/module-signatures.md, and a test requires it. 'optional': the renderer may add the flag or not, and a test accepts both. Only the flags on a value that the input's form lacks are optional, because the cause for those is open (S-12(b), named by T032).",
    "A flag that the renderer adds and that is not listed is a defect of one side: the list is complete for the cases here."
  ],
  "identity": {
    "for_findings_present_in_both": true,
    "keys_equal": [
      "run1",
      "run2",
      "run3"
    ],
    "note": "every carried finding keeps its SARIF identity fields across the regroup, and the unchanged re-run keeps them and its values; the properties that name a baseline state or a score source may differ with the status",
    "rerun_matches": {
      "run3": "run2"
    }
  },
  "notes": [
    "Three runs in sequence, each writing its outputs next to its own threats.md (--out run1, then run2, then run3), so that each run's baseline.source finds the last run's output: run1 reads baseline/, run2 reads run1/, run3 reads run2/. run1 and run2's baselines are therefore the renderer's own output, and only the first baseline is a fixture file.",
    "Run 1 scores the legacy baseline again with the baseline's groups, CG-1 = [I-1, LLM-1] and CG-2 = [R-1, AG-1]. Nothing is wrong and nothing is flagged: it is the first renderer run, and the scores it carries are the ones run 2 must not move.",
    "Run 2 regroups. Correlation now puts T-1, an ungrouped Medium finding, first in CG-1, so the group's primary changes from I-1 (High) to T-1. No carried finding's score, band or SLA changes because of the regroup alone (US-5 #6). I-1 and LLM-1 are UNCHANGED peers whose carried score differs from the new primary's: they keep it and are flagged divergent:composite_score:primary=T-1. D-1 (NEW) and E-1 (UPDATED) are peers that copy T-1's vector and scores; E-1 keeps its owner and, because its band changes, restarts its clock.",
    "Run 3 re-runs run 2's file with every status UNCHANGED, on run 2's output. It keeps every key and value of run 2, and the divergences stay flagged, since I-1 and LLM-1 still differ from T-1. D-1 and E-1 are now carried peers that equal their primary.",
    "S-7: the correlation outcome of the pair (which findings group, and each group's primary) is the same whatever the SARIF recipe does; 'groups' lists it per run, primary first.",
    "baseline/risk-scores.sarif is a pre-fix file: its hashes are the legacy ones, which a renderer never copies and never matches on."
  ],
  "populator_fixed_point": true,
